repository-code: 'https://github.com/numpy/numpy'
url: 'https://numpy.org/'
abstract: >-
  NumPy is the fundamental package for scientific computing
  in Python. It is a Python library that provides a
  multidimensional array object, various derived objects
  (such as masked arrays and matrices), and an assortment of
  routines for fast operations on arrays, including
  mathematical, logical, shape manipulation, sorting,
  selecting, I/O, discrete Fourier transforms, basic linear
  algebra, basic statistical operations, random simulation
  and much more.
